//? Title: Continuing robot-arm fruit sorting
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

> Continuing robot-arm fruit sorting

The robot now works in a **continuing environment**. Fruit appears according to
a Poisson process while the belt keeps moving and the arm keeps its joint pose
between picks. The environment has no episode horizon; the video below is a
single, uninterrupted **60-second observation window** of a frozen trained policy.
The earlier arrival, episodic RL and varied-fruit classification examples remain
in [the episodic report|file:robot_fruit_episodic.mepml].

>> Arrivals, deadlines and physical outcomes

The demonstration uses **0.12 fruit per second**, or 7.2 arrivals per minute in
expectation. Exponential inter-arrival times are independent of the arm's
availability, chosen actions and appearance randomness. There is no minimum
spacing, busy-arm pause, source queue or admission delay. Poisson bursts can
produce several fruit at once. Every fruit receives a random belt position,
orientation, size, skin and one of six prototypes per class.

The friction-driven belt runs continuously at **0.22 metres per second**.
The arm can intercept at X=0.04 or X=0.16 m. Unhandled fruit passing X=0.30 m
counts as missed. Misses also include failed releases and capacity overflow. Fruit still travelling, held or falling at the end of a
measurement window remains **in progress**, and is reported separately.
A correct sort requires a dynamic fruit to settle with physical floor support
inside the correct bin: apples in red and bananas in yellow.

The bins automatically clear completed fruit after two seconds so the world
can run indefinitely with bounded memory. The active-body limit is 32;
an arrival at capacity is counted as an overflow miss, rather than postponed.
Births are inserted within one 1/240-second tick of their exact scheduled time.

>> Learning to keep up

A hierarchical controller learns five duration-varying choices: wait, intercept
the leading fruit at either gate, or intercept the second-leading fruit at
either gate. It observes queue size, leading position, spacing, arm side and
pending releases. It cannot see future arrivals or use true fruit labels to
choose a bin. Fixed IK options approach, time the descent, close the gripper,
lift, traverse and release, with bounded joint/finger rates and fixture guards.
This trains scheduling and interception decisions; it does not learn motor
torques or replace the existing idealized grasp and arm-collision assumptions.

The option reward is five times correct placements, minus five times wrong
placements, minus three times misses, minus 0.02 per elapsed second and 0.25
per failed attempt. Q-learning discounts the next-state value by
`0.995^elapsed_seconds`, so a slow option has its actual time cost. Training
uses **8,192 independent continuing windows of at least 120 simulated seconds**,
with randomized arrival rates from 0.10 to 0.22 fruit/s. Windows are truncated
for sampling; their final values bootstrap rather than receive a terminal reward.

The fast training model preserves arrival scheduling, servo durations, fixture
guards and rewards, while approximating belt transport and bin settling and
omitting fruit-to-fruit contacts. Its perception-error channel is calibrated
using classifier validation data. **It is a training proxy, not the final
physics simulation.** Power-of-two checkpoints are compared on twelve separate
full-physics validation streams before the final policy is selected.

>> Adapting wrist vision to moving pickups

The rigid wrist camera renders the actual multi-fruit scene. Registered RGB
background subtraction finds visible components; a projected tracked target
position associates the intended component. This association and the motor
controller use privileged geometry. The box itself comes from RGB differences,
and MobileNet receives the unannotated padded RGB crop. Its prediction alone
selects red or yellow. Empty crops remain unknown and never use a true-label
fallback. Green video boxes show the current target's visible component.

The previous MobileNet checkpoint is fine-tuned for forty epochs on moving
pickup views: 512 images from prototypes 0–3, 128 validation images from
prototype 4, and 128 test images from prototype 5. Classes/prototypes are
balanced and stream seeds are disjoint. Brightness and grayscale augmentation
remain enabled. Validation loss selects the vision checkpoint; test images
never supply gradients or select a checkpoint.

The final comparison uses sixteen independent two-minute streams with actual
RGB inference and full 240 Hz physics. The learned scheduler and both fixed
oldest-first baselines see identical Poisson arrival streams. Counts are taken
at the exact window boundary, including unresolved work. The video seed is
fixed before training, and its minute includes all idle periods, misses,
classification mistakes and unfinished work—there is no success montage.

Run `just playground` to train and build everything. Once learning has completed,
`DATAMUNGE_STREAM_REPLAY=1 just playground` reloads its frozen checkpoints and
regenerates the evaluation video. The simulator itself can keep stepping forever;
only recording stops at one minute.

```{cpp, results="markdown", nix-shell="git+file:../../..#cpp", cmd="c++ -std=c++23 -O2 {file} -o {bin} $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge) && OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 {bin}"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/nn/parallel.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <array>
#include <cstdlib>
#include <fstream>
#include <iostream>
#include <iomanip>
#include <numeric>
#include <sstream>
#include <stdexcept>
namespace s=dm::sim;namespace n=dm::nn;namespace c=dm::cad;
namespace fs=std::filesystem;
constexpr double arrival_rate=.12;
constexpr std::uint64_t video_seed=2026113001ULL;
constexpr int fps=15,video_seconds=60;
const std::string directory="build/fruit_stream/";

n::Tensor rgb(const c::RenderResult& image){
 std::vector<float> pixels;pixels.reserve(image.width*image.height*3);
 for(std::size_t i=0;i<image.rgba.size();i+=4)for(int k=0;k<3;++k)pixels.push_back(image.rgba[i+k]/255.f);
 return n::from_vector(pixels,{1,image.height,image.width,3});
}
const s::StreamFruit& target(const s::StreamFrame& frame,std::uint64_t id){
 auto it=std::find_if(frame.fruit.begin(),frame.fruit.end(),[&](const auto& p){return p.id==id;});
 if(it==frame.fruit.end())throw std::runtime_error("Recorded target is absent");return *it;
}
c::Vec3d centre(const s::StreamFruit& p){return {p.body.position[0],p.body.position[2],p.body.position[1]};}
std::uint64_t unresolved(const s::StreamFrame& f){
 return f.counts.arrivals-f.counts.correct-f.counts.wrong-f.counts.missed;
}
struct Data {n::Tensor images,labels;};
// These are supervised synthetic image-collection streams, not evaluation runs.
// Quotas use labels, while the exploratory collection routes alternate by ID.
Data collect(s::FruitStreamEnvironment& env,s::DevArmWristCamera& camera,std::uint64_t first_seed,
             int lo,int hi,int quota,const std::string& split,std::ostream& manifest){
 std::array<std::array<int,6>,2> counts{};std::vector<float> pixels;std::vector<std::int64_t> labels;
 const int needed=2*(hi-lo+1)*quota;std::uint64_t current_seed=first_seed;
 env.set_perception([&](const s::StreamFrame& frame,std::uint64_t id){
   const auto& p=target(frame,id);const int truth=p.body.kind==s::FruitKind::Apple?0:1;int prototype=p.body.appearance.prototype;
   if(prototype>=lo&&prototype<=hi&&counts[truth][prototype]<quota){
     const auto input=camera.inspect_actors(frame.arm,env.fruit_scene(frame),centre(p));
     if(!input.crop.rgba.empty()){
       auto v=rgb(input.crop).to_vector<float>();pixels.insert(pixels.end(),v.begin(),v.end());labels.push_back(truth);++counts[truth][prototype];
       manifest<<std::format("{},{},{},{},{},{},{:.8f},{:.8f},{:.8f},{:.8f},{:.8f},{},{},{},{}\n",split,current_seed,id,p.seed,truth,prototype,frame.time,p.body.position[0],p.body.position[2],p.body.appearance.yaw,p.body.appearance.scale,input.box.x,input.box.y,input.box.width,input.box.height);
       if(labels.size()%128==0)std::cerr<<split<<" moving-view crops "<<labels.size()<<"/"<<needed<<'\n';
     }
   }
   return s::StreamPrediction{int(id%2),.5}; // independent of the true label
 });
 for(;int(labels.size())<needed;++current_seed){
   auto f=env.reset(current_seed,arrival_rate);std::size_t decisions=0;
   while(f.time<120&&int(labels.size())<needed)
     f=env.step(++decisions%3==0?s::StreamAction::LateFront:s::StreamAction::EarlyFront).frame;
 }
 env.set_perception({});
 return {n::from_vector(pixels,{needed,64,64,3}),n::from_vector(labels)};
}
struct Vision {
 s::FruitStreamEnvironment& env;s::DevArmWristCamera& camera;n::MobileNetClassifier& model;
 std::ostream& log;std::uint64_t seed{0};std::string mode;
 s::StreamPrediction operator()(const s::StreamFrame& f,std::uint64_t id){
   if(f.training_proxy)throw std::runtime_error("Actual evaluation must use full physics");
   const auto& p=target(f,id);auto input=camera.inspect_actors(f.arm,env.fruit_scene(f),centre(p));
   s::StreamPrediction prediction;
   if(!input.crop.rgba.empty()){const auto probabilities=model.predict(rgb(input.crop)).to_vector<float>();prediction.label=probabilities[1]>probabilities[0]?1:0;prediction.confidence=probabilities[prediction.label];}
   if(f.time<=(mode=="video"?video_seconds:120))
     log<<std::format("{},{},{},{:.8f},{},{},{:.9f},{},{},{},{}\n",mode,seed,id,f.time,int(p.body.kind),prediction.label,prediction.confidence,input.box.x,input.box.y,input.box.width,input.box.height);
   return prediction; // an empty crop stays unknown; there is no true-class fallback
 }
};
s::StreamFrame window(s::FruitStreamEnvironment& env,std::uint64_t seed,double rate,double seconds,
                      const std::function<s::StreamAction(std::size_t)>& policy){
 s::StreamFrame endpoint;
 env.record([&](const auto& f){if(f.time<=seconds+1e-9)endpoint=f;},1);
 auto f=env.reset(seed,rate);
 while(f.time<seconds)f=env.step(policy(f.state)).frame;
 env.record({});
 if(std::abs(endpoint.time-seconds)>1e-8)throw std::runtime_error("Evaluation did not capture the exact horizon");
 return endpoint; // final option may complete later; its future outcomes are not counted
}
struct Totals {
 std::uint64_t arrivals{0},correct{0},wrong{0},missed{0},pending{0},inspections{0},classified{0},unknown{0};
 void add(const s::StreamFrame& f){const auto& x=f.counts;arrivals+=x.arrivals;correct+=x.correct;wrong+=x.wrong;missed+=x.missed;pending+=unresolved(f);inspections+=x.inspections;classified+=x.classification_correct;unknown+=x.unknown;}
};
void append(c::Scene& scene,c::Scene extra){
 int base=int(scene.meshes.size()),tex=int(scene.textures.size());
 for(auto& m:extra.meshes)scene.meshes.push_back(std::move(m));for(auto& t:extra.textures)scene.textures.push_back(std::move(t));
 for(auto o:extra.objects){o.mesh_index+=base;o.parent=-1;for(int* p:{&o.texture_index,&o.normal_map_index,&o.roughness_map_index,&o.metallic_map_index})if(*p>=0)*p+=tex;scene.AddObject(o);}
}
void box(c::RenderResult& image,const s::ImageBox& b){
 for(int y=b.y;y<b.y+b.height;++y)for(int x=b.x;x<b.x+b.width;++x){
  if(x>b.x+1&&x<b.x+b.width-2&&y>b.y+1&&y<b.y+b.height-2)continue;
  auto i=4*(y*image.width+x);image.rgba[i]=30;image.rgba[i+1]=245;image.rgba[i+2]=120;
 }
}
void panel(c::RenderResult& image,int x,int y,int width,int height){
 for(int yy=y;yy<y+height;++yy)for(int xx=x;xx<x+width;++xx){auto i=4*(yy*image.width+xx);for(int k=0;k<3;++k)image.rgba[i+k]=static_cast<unsigned char>(.18*image.rgba[i+k]+.82*20);}
}
void composite(c::RenderResult& dest,const c::RenderResult& actors){
 for(std::size_t i=0;i<dest.depth.size();++i)if(actors.depth[i]<dest.depth[i]){
   std::copy_n(actors.rgba.begin()+4*i,4,dest.rgba.begin()+4*i);dest.depth[i]=actors.depth[i];
 }
}
void copy_artifacts(){
 for(const std::string name:{"sorting.mp4","poster.png","inspection.png","camera_samples.png","vision_learning.svg","controller_learning.svg","load_curve.svg","mobile.npz","policy.txt","images.csv","vision_training.csv","controller_training.csv","controller_validation.csv","evaluation.csv","load_evaluation.csv","perception.csv","video_perception.csv","evaluation_summary.txt","trajectory.csv","fruit_trajectory.csv","metadata.txt","metrics.json"})
   if(fs::exists(directory+name))fs::copy_file(directory+name,"figures/fruit_stream_"+name,fs::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
}
int main(){
 n::set_num_threads(1);fs::create_directories(directory+"frames");fs::create_directories("figures");
 const bool replay=std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_STREAM_REPLAY")!=nullptr;
 const bool learn_only=std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_STREAM_LEARN_ONLY")!=nullptr;
 if(replay&&learn_only)throw std::invalid_argument("Choose learning or replay, not both");
 const auto assets=dm::datasets::fetch("rebot_devarm","../../../build/cad-assets/rebot");
 const auto urdf=(fs::path(assets)/"Rebot_Arm_description/DM/urdf/ReBot_Arm_DM.urdf").string();
 std::size_t selected_epoch=0,selected_window=0;int vision_correct=0;
 double trained_seconds=0;std::array<double,2> errors{};
 if(!replay){
   s::FruitStreamOptions collection_options;collection_options.training_proxy=true;
   s::FruitStreamEnvironment collection(urdf,collection_options);s::DevArmWristCamera camera(collection.arm_model(),128,95);
   std::ofstream manifest(directory+"images.csv");manifest<<"split,stream_seed,id,fruit_seed,true_class,prototype,time,x,y,yaw,scale,box_x,box_y,box_width,box_height\n";
   const auto train=collect(collection,camera,6000000000000ULL,0,3,64,"train",manifest);
   const auto validation=collect(collection,camera,7000000000000ULL,4,4,64,"validation",manifest);
   const auto test=collect(collection,camera,8000000000000ULL,5,5,64,"test",manifest);manifest.close();
   n::save_image_grid(n::slice_axis(test.images,0,0,24),directory+"camera_samples.png",8,0,1,2,.9,2);
   auto mobile=n::MobileNetClassifier::load("figures/fruit_vision_mobilenet.npz");
   n::MobileClassifierOptions fit;fit.epochs=40;fit.learning_rate=.001;fit.grayscale_probability=.25;fit.seed=20261109;
   std::cerr<<"Fine-tuning actual moving-view RGB classifier\n";
   const auto fitted=mobile.fit(train.images,train.labels,validation.images,validation.labels,fit);selected_epoch=fitted.selected_epoch;
   mobile.save(directory+"mobile.npz");auto loaded=n::MobileNetClassifier::load(directory+"mobile.npz");
   if(n::max(n::abs(loaded.predict(test.images)-mobile.predict(test.images))).item()>1e-7)throw std::runtime_error("Vision checkpoint changed probabilities");
   auto val_pred=n::argmax(loaded.predict(validation.images),-1).to_vector<std::int64_t>();
   auto val_truth=validation.labels.to_vector<std::int64_t>();std::array<int,2> val_count{},val_wrong{};
   for(std::size_t i=0;i<val_pred.size();++i){++val_count[val_truth[i]];val_wrong[val_truth[i]]+=val_pred[i]!=val_truth[i];}
   for(int k=0;k<2;++k)errors[k]=double(val_wrong[k]+1)/(val_count[k]+2); // validation-only smoothed error channel
   const auto test_pred=n::argmax(loaded.predict(test.images),-1).to_vector<std::int64_t>();const auto truth=test.labels.to_vector<std::int64_t>();
   for(std::size_t i=0;i<truth.size();++i)vision_correct+=test_pred[i]==truth[i];
   std::ofstream history(directory+"vision_training.csv");history<<"epoch,training_loss,validation_loss,validation_accuracy\n";
   std::vector<double> epochs,train_loss,val_loss;
   for(const auto& e:fitted.history){history<<std::format("{},{:.9f},{:.9f},{:.9f}\n",e.epoch,e.training_loss,e.validation_loss,e.validation_accuracy);epochs.push_back(e.epoch);train_loss.push_back(e.training_loss);val_loss.push_back(e.validation_loss);}history.close();
   auto learning=dm::Plot().lines(epochs,train_loss,"Training",dm::RGB{37,99,235});learning.lines(epochs,val_loss,"Validation",dm::RGB{220,38,38});
   learning.set_title("MobileNet adaptation to moving pickups").set_xlab("Epoch").set_ylab("Cross entropy");learning.size(900,340).save_svg(directory+"vision_learning.svg");
   s::FruitStreamOptions training_options;training_options.training_proxy=true;training_options.training_error=errors;
   s::FruitStreamEnvironment trainer(urdf,training_options);s::StreamTrainingOptions training;training.rollouts=8192;
   std::cerr<<"Training scheduler over 8192 continuing windows\n";
   auto learned=s::train_fruit_stream(trainer,training);trained_seconds=std::accumulate(learned.seconds.begin(),learned.seconds.end(),0.);
   std::ofstream csv(directory+"controller_training.csv");csv<<"window,seconds,arrivals,correct,wrong,missed,return\n";
   for(std::size_t k=0;k<learned.counts.size();++k){const auto& x=learned.counts[k];csv<<std::format("{},{:.8f},{},{},{},{},{:.9f}\n",k+1,learned.seconds[k],x.arrivals,x.correct,x.wrong,x.missed,learned.returns[k]);}csv.close();
   // Select a frozen checkpoint on independent full-physics validation streams.
   s::FruitStreamOptions physical_options;physical_options.training_error=errors;s::FruitStreamEnvironment physical(urdf,physical_options);
   double best=-1e100;std::vector<double> hours,correct_rate,miss_rate;std::ofstream valid(directory+"controller_validation.csv");valid<<"training_windows,training_seconds,arrivals,correct,wrong,missed,pending,score\n";
   for(std::size_t k=0;k<learned.snapshots.size();++k){const auto& candidate=learned.snapshots[k];Totals total;
     for(int stream=0;stream<12;++stream)total.add(window(physical,90000000000ULL+stream,arrival_rate,120,[&](auto state){return candidate.action(state);}));
     double score=5.*total.correct-5.*total.wrong-3.*total.missed;
     auto completed=learned.snapshot_windows[k];double seconds=std::accumulate(learned.seconds.begin(),learned.seconds.begin()+completed,0.);
     valid<<std::format("{},{:.8f},{},{},{},{},{},{:.8f}\n",completed,seconds,total.arrivals,total.correct,total.wrong,total.missed,total.pending,score);
     hours.push_back(seconds/3600);correct_rate.push_back(total.correct/24.);miss_rate.push_back(total.missed/24.);
     if(score>best){best=score;selected_window=completed;candidate.save(directory+"policy.txt");}
     std::cerr<<"Physical validation "<<completed<<" windows: correct "<<total.correct<<", missed "<<total.missed<<'\n';
   }valid.close();
   auto control=dm::Plot().lines(hours,correct_rate,"Correct sorts",dm::RGB{15,140,100});control.lines(hours,miss_rate,"Missed",dm::RGB{220,38,38});
   control.set_title("Frozen scheduler: full-physics validation").set_xlab("Simulated training hours").set_ylab("Fruit per minute");control.size(900,340).save_svg(directory+"controller_learning.svg");
   std::ofstream metadata(directory+"metadata.txt");metadata<<"DATAMUNGE_STREAM_RUN 1\n"<<selected_epoch<<' '<<selected_window<<' '<<vision_correct<<' '<<std::setprecision(17)<<trained_seconds<<' '<<errors[0]<<' '<<errors[1]<<'\n';
 }
 // Explicit replay loads the completed training run; normal builds train above.
 std::ifstream metadata(directory+"metadata.txt");std::string magic;int version=0;
 if(!(metadata>>magic>>version>>selected_epoch>>selected_window>>vision_correct>>trained_seconds>>errors[0]>>errors[1])||magic!="DATAMUNGE_STREAM_RUN"||version!=1)throw std::runtime_error("Missing completed training metadata");
 auto classifier=n::MobileNetClassifier::load(directory+"mobile.npz");const auto policy=s::StreamPolicy::load(directory+"policy.txt");
 s::FruitStreamEnvironment env(urdf);s::DevArmWristCamera wrist(env.arm_model(),128,95);
 std::ofstream perception; if(!replay){perception.open(directory+"perception.csv");perception<<"mode,stream_seed,id,time,true_class,predicted_class,confidence,box_x,box_y,box_width,box_height\n";}
 Vision vision{env,wrist,classifier,perception};env.set_perception([&](const auto& f,auto id){return vision(f,id);});
 std::array<Totals,3> totals{};
 if(!replay){
   std::ofstream evaluation(directory+"evaluation.csv");evaluation<<"method,seed,rate,seconds,arrivals,correct,wrong,missed,pending,inspections,classified,unknown\n";
   for(int method=0;method<3;++method)for(int k=0;k<16;++k){vision.seed=91000000000ULL+k;vision.mode=method==0?"trained":method==1?"early-oldest":"late-oldest";
     auto f=window(env,vision.seed,arrival_rate,120,[&](auto state){return method==0?policy.action(state):method==1?s::StreamAction::EarlyFront:s::StreamAction::LateFront;});totals[method].add(f);
     const auto& x=f.counts;evaluation<<std::format("{},{},{:.4f},120,{},{},{},{},{},{},{},{}\n",vision.mode,vision.seed,arrival_rate,x.arrivals,x.correct,x.wrong,x.missed,unresolved(f),x.inspections,x.classification_correct,x.unknown);
   }evaluation.close();
   std::ofstream evaluation_summary(directory+"evaluation_summary.txt");for(const auto& t:totals)evaluation_summary<<t.arrivals<<' '<<t.correct<<' '<<t.wrong<<' '<<t.missed<<' '<<t.pending<<' '<<t.inspections<<' '<<t.classified<<' '<<t.unknown<<'\n';evaluation_summary.close();
   // Load tests isolate scheduling under the validation-calibrated error channel.
   s::FruitStreamOptions stress_options;stress_options.training_error=errors;s::FruitStreamEnvironment stress(urdf,stress_options);
   std::vector<double> load,learn_correct,fifo_correct,learn_missed,fifo_missed;std::ofstream stress_csv(directory+"load_evaluation.csv");stress_csv<<"method,seed,rate,seconds,arrivals,correct,wrong,missed,pending\n";
   for(double rate:{.08,.12,.18,.24}){load.push_back(rate*60);std::array<Totals,2> scored;
     for(int method=0;method<2;++method)for(int k=0;k<8;++k){auto seed=92000000000ULL+k;auto f=window(stress,seed,rate,120,[&](auto state){return method==0?policy.action(state):s::StreamAction::EarlyFront;});scored[method].add(f);
       stress_csv<<std::format("{},{},{:.4f},120,{},{},{},{},{}\n",method==0?"trained":"early-oldest",seed,rate,f.counts.arrivals,f.counts.correct,f.counts.wrong,f.counts.missed,unresolved(f));}
     learn_correct.push_back(scored[0].correct/16.);fifo_correct.push_back(scored[1].correct/16.);learn_missed.push_back(scored[0].missed/16.);fifo_missed.push_back(scored[1].missed/16.);
   }stress_csv.close();
   auto throughput=dm::Plot().lines(load,learn_correct,"Learned",dm::RGB{37,99,235});throughput.lines(load,fifo_correct,"Early oldest",dm::RGB{140,140,140});throughput.set_title("Correct sorting throughput").set_xlab("Expected arrivals per minute").set_ylab("Correct sorts per minute");
   auto misses=dm::Plot().lines(load,learn_missed,"Learned",dm::RGB{37,99,235});misses.lines(load,fifo_missed,"Early oldest",dm::RGB{140,140,140});misses.set_title("Missed fruit").set_xlab("Expected arrivals per minute").set_ylab("Misses per minute");
   auto layout=dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(throughput).add(misses).fit_panels();dm::plot(layout).size(1050,340).save_svg(directory+"load_curve.svg");
 } else {
   std::ifstream summary(directory+"evaluation_summary.txt");for(auto& t:totals)if(!(summary>>t.arrivals>>t.correct>>t.wrong>>t.missed>>t.pending>>t.inspections>>t.classified>>t.unknown))throw std::runtime_error("Missing frozen evaluation summary");
 }
 if(learn_only){perception.flush();copy_artifacts();std::cerr<<"LEARNING COMPLETE: vision "<<vision_correct<<"/128; selected controller window "<<selected_window<<"; trained actual RGB correct "<<totals[0].correct<<" vs early "<<totals[1].correct<<" vs late "<<totals[2].correct<<'\n';return 0;}
 // One unselected seed, one uninterrupted real-time minute: no episode montage.
 std::ofstream video_log(directory+"video_perception.csv");video_log<<"mode,stream_seed,id,time,true_class,predicted_class,confidence,box_x,box_y,box_width,box_height\n";
 Vision video_vision{env,wrist,classifier,video_log};video_vision.seed=video_seed;video_vision.mode="video";
 env.set_perception([&](const auto& frame,auto id){return video_vision(frame,id);});
 std::vector<s::StreamFrame> frames;
 env.record([&](const auto& f){if(f.time<=video_seconds+1e-9)frames.push_back(f);},fps);
 auto f=env.reset(video_seed,arrival_rate);
 while(f.time<video_seconds)f=env.step(policy.action(f.state)).frame;
 env.record({});
 if(frames.size()!=fps*video_seconds+1||std::abs(frames.back().time-video_seconds)>1e-8)throw std::runtime_error("Video horizon/sample count mismatch");
 const auto endpoint=frames.back();frames.resize(fps*video_seconds);
 for(const auto& x:frames)if(x.training_proxy||x.synthetic_perception)throw std::runtime_error("Final video must use full physics and actual RGB predictions");
 c::Camera overview;overview.position={-1.35,-.6,5};overview.target={-.1,0,.7};overview.projection=c::Projection::Orthographic;overview.ortho_height=1.95;
 c::RenderOptions options;options.width=960;options.height=640;options.background={.91f,.94f,.96f,1};
 auto scenery=env.arm_model().static_scene();c::Light key;key.direction={-1,-2,3};key.intensity=1;scenery.AddLight(key);c::Light fill;fill.direction={1,1,2};fill.intensity=.35f;scenery.AddLight(fill);
 const auto background=c::render(scenery,overview,options);auto base=background;std::array<double,6> last_joints{};double last_finger=-1;
 std::ofstream trajectory(directory+"trajectory.csv");trajectory<<"frame,time,target,arrivals,correct,wrong,missed,pending,grasped,q1,q2,q3,q4,q5,q6,finger\n";
 std::ofstream fruit_trace(directory+"fruit_trajectory.csv");fruit_trace<<"frame,time,id,seed,scheduled_arrival,status,prediction,confidence,x,y,z,qw,qx,qy,qz\n";
 bool saved_inspection=false;
 for(std::size_t k=0;k<frames.size();++k){const auto& x=frames[k];
   if(x.arm.joints!=last_joints||x.arm.finger!=last_finger){auto arm=env.arm_model().robot_scene(x.arm);append(arm,wrist.housing(x.arm));arm.lights=scenery.lights;base=background;composite(base,c::render(arm,overview,options));last_joints=x.arm.joints;last_finger=x.arm.finger;}
   auto actors=env.fruit_scene(x);actors.lights=scenery.lights;auto image=base;composite(image,c::render(actors,overview,options));
   c::RenderResult live;int prediction=-1;double confidence=0;
   auto focus=std::find_if(x.fruit.begin(),x.fruit.end(),[&](const auto& p){return p.id==x.target;});
   if(focus!=x.fruit.end()){auto inspected=wrist.inspect_actors(x.arm,actors,centre(*focus));box(inspected.rgb,inspected.box);live=std::move(inspected.rgb);prediction=focus->prediction;confidence=focus->confidence;}
   else live=wrist.capture_actors(x.arm,actors);
   constexpr int left=684,top=20,scale=2,border=5;
   std::array<unsigned char,3> color=prediction<0?std::array<unsigned char,3>{145,160,175}:prediction==0?std::array<unsigned char,3>{215,40,35}:std::array<unsigned char,3>{250,210,35};
   for(int yy=-border;yy<128*scale+border;++yy)for(int xx=-border;xx<128*scale+border;++xx){auto i=4*((top+yy)*image.width+left+xx);bool edge=xx<0||yy<0||xx>=128*scale||yy>=128*scale;for(int ch=0;ch<3;++ch)image.rgba[i+ch]=edge?color[ch]:live.rgba[4*((yy/scale)*128+xx/scale)+ch];image.rgba[i+3]=255;}
   panel(image,679,281,266,26);c::draw_text(image,prediction<0?"WRIST - NOT CLASSIFIED":std::format("{} P {:.2f}",prediction==0?"APPLE":"BANANA",confidence),690,288,2);
   panel(image,15,570,650,58);c::draw_text(image,std::format("T {:.1f} S  POISSON {:.2f}/S  ARRIVED {}",x.time,arrival_rate,x.counts.arrivals),25,578,2);
   c::draw_text(image,std::format("SORTED {}  WRONG {}  MISSED {}  ACTIVE {}",x.counts.correct,x.counts.wrong,x.counts.missed,unresolved(x)),25,602,2);
   image.save(std::format("{}frames/{:05}.png",directory,k));
   if(k+1==frames.size())image.save(directory+"poster.png");if(!saved_inspection&&prediction>=0){image.save(directory+"inspection.png");saved_inspection=true;}
   trajectory<<std::format("{},{:.8f},{},{},{},{},{},{},{}",k,x.time,x.target,x.counts.arrivals,x.counts.correct,x.counts.wrong,x.counts.missed,unresolved(x),int(x.arm.grasped));for(double q:x.arm.joints)trajectory<<std::format(",{:.9f}",q);trajectory<<std::format(",{:.9f}\n",x.arm.finger);
   for(const auto& p:x.fruit){fruit_trace<<std::format("{},{:.8f},{},{},{:.9f},{},{},{:.9f},{:.9f},{:.9f},{:.9f}",k,x.time,p.id,p.seed,p.arrival,int(p.status),p.prediction,p.confidence,p.body.position[0],p.body.position[2],p.body.position[1]);for(double v:p.body.rotation)fruit_trace<<std::format(",{:.9f}",v);fruit_trace<<'\n';}
   if(k%150==0)std::cerr<<"Render "<<k<<"/"<<frames.size()<<" frames\n";
 }
 trajectory.close();fruit_trace.close();perception.close();video_log.close();
 const auto encode="ffmpeg -hide_banner -loglevel error -y -framerate 15 -i "+directory+"frames/%05d.png -frames:v 900 -an -c:v libx264 -profile:v baseline -level 3.1 -bf 0 -g 30 -preset fast -crf 19 -pix_fmt yuv420p -movflags +faststart "+directory+"sorting.mp4";
 if(std::system(encode.c_str())!=0)throw std::runtime_error("Video encoding failed");
 std::ofstream metrics(directory+"metrics.json");metrics<<"{\"arrival_rate\":"<<arrival_rate<<",\"video_seed\":"<<video_seed<<",\"video_seconds\":60,\"fps\":15,\"frames\":900,\"training_windows\":8192,\"training_seconds\":"<<std::setprecision(17)<<trained_seconds<<",\"selected_controller_window\":"<<selected_window<<",\"selected_vision_epoch\":"<<selected_epoch<<",\"vision_test_correct\":"<<vision_correct<<",\"vision_test_total\":128,\"video_arrivals\":"<<endpoint.counts.arrivals<<",\"video_correct\":"<<endpoint.counts.correct<<",\"video_wrong\":"<<endpoint.counts.wrong<<",\"video_missed\":"<<endpoint.counts.missed<<",\"video_pending\":"<<unresolved(endpoint)<<",\"actual_rgb_evaluation_arrivals\":"<<totals[0].arrivals<<",\"actual_rgb_evaluation_correct\":"<<totals[0].correct<<",\"actual_rgb_evaluation_wrong\":"<<totals[0].wrong<<",\"actual_rgb_evaluation_missed\":"<<totals[0].missed<<",\"actual_rgb_evaluation_pending\":"<<totals[0].pending<<",\"early_oldest_correct\":"<<totals[1].correct<<",\"early_oldest_missed\":"<<totals[1].missed<<",\"late_oldest_correct\":"<<totals[2].correct<<",\"late_oldest_missed\":"<<totals[2].missed<<",\"full_physics_video\":true,\"actual_rgb_video\":true}\n";metrics.close();copy_artifacts();
 if(replay)std::println("Replaying the completed training run and its frozen checkpoints.\n");
 std::println("The scheduler trained for **{:.1f} simulated hours** across **8,192 continuing windows**. Independent full-physics validation selected checkpoint **{}**. Moving-view MobileNet classified **{}/128** held-out-prototype crops correctly.\n",trained_seconds/3600,selected_window,vision_correct);
 std::println("Across **16 independent two-minute streams with actual wrist RGB**, the learned scheduler correctly sorted **{}**, versus **{}** for early-oldest and **{}** for late-oldest. Missed fruit: **{}**, **{}**, and **{}**, respectively. All methods use the same Poisson arrival streams.\n",totals[0].correct,totals[1].correct,totals[2].correct,totals[0].missed,totals[1].missed,totals[2].missed);
 std::println("The uninterrupted **60-second** video uses seed `{}` at **{:.2f} fruit/s**. At 60 seconds: **{} arrivals**, **{} correct**, **{} wrong**, **{} missed**, **{} still in progress**. The belt keeps running; there are no cuts, speed-ups or between-pick resets.\n",video_seed,arrival_rate,endpoint.counts.arrivals,endpoint.counts.correct,endpoint.counts.wrong,endpoint.counts.missed,unresolved(endpoint));
 std::println("\\video(figures/fruit_stream_sorting.mp4)");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Replaying the completed training run and its frozen checkpoints.

The scheduler trained for **276.1 simulated hours** across **8,192 continuing windows**. Independent full-physics validation selected checkpoint **512**. Moving-view MobileNet classified **121/128** held-out-prototype crops correctly.

Across **16 independent two-minute streams with actual wrist RGB**, the learned scheduler correctly sorted **155**, versus **149** for early-oldest and **97** for late-oldest. Missed fruit: **66**, **73**, and **133**, respectively. All methods use the same Poisson arrival streams.

The uninterrupted **60-second** video uses seed `2026113001` at **0.12 fruit/s**. At 60 seconds: **4 arrivals**, **3 correct**, **0 wrong**, **1 missed**, **0 still in progress**. The belt keeps running; there are no cuts, speed-ups or between-pick resets.

\video(figures/fruit_stream_sorting.mp4)
// result_end

\caption(One uninterrupted real-time minute of the frozen trained scheduler, with continuous Poisson arrivals and actual wrist RGB classification. The HUD reports arrivals, correct/wrong placements, misses and active work. Green boxes show visible target regions; gray means not yet classified, red means predicted apple, and yellow means predicted banana. Completed fruit clears from the bins after two seconds.)
\alttext(A robot repeatedly intercepts fruit on a continuously moving conveyor and sorts it into red and yellow bins. Multiple fruit can coexist. A wrist-camera inset shows target bounds and current class predictions, while live counters show misses and unfinished work.)

[Open the one-minute video|file:figures/fruit_stream_sorting.mp4]
or its [final frame|file:figures/fruit_stream_poster.png].

\image(figures/fruit_stream_inspection.png)
\caption(A classification made at an actual moving-pickup pose. The box and text are display annotations and never enter MobileNet.)
\alttext(The continuing conveyor workcell with its live wrist-camera crop and prediction overlay.)

\image(figures/fruit_stream_camera_samples.png)
\caption(Unannotated moving-view classifier inputs from held-out prototype 5. These include position, orientation, color and occlusion variation.)
\alttext(Three rows of eight varied fruit crops captured from the wrist camera.)

\image(figures/fruit_stream_vision_learning.svg)
\caption(MobileNet fine-tuning on moving-pickup images. Validation prototype 4 selects the checkpoint before test prototype 5 is evaluated.)
\alttext(Training and validation cross entropy across forty epochs.)

\image(figures/fruit_stream_controller_learning.svg)
\caption(Frozen scheduler checkpoints on full-physics validation streams, using the validation-calibrated perception-error channel. This figure selects the scheduling checkpoint; the final comparison and video use actual MobileNet RGB inference.)
\alttext(Correct sorts and misses per minute as simulated training time increases.)

\image(figures/fruit_stream_load_curve.svg)
\caption(Full-physics throughput and total misses across increasing Poisson arrival rates, using the same validation-calibrated perception channel for both controllers. Bursts and limited service capacity produce more losses at high rates. This controlled load test is separate from the actual-RGB evaluation.)
\alttext(Two panels compare correct sorting throughput and missed fruit per minute for learned and early-oldest scheduling as arrivals increase.)

